      "Agreements between clients and service providers are independent from the app. The company is not responsible for service outcomes.",
      "Usage is strictly personal. It is prohibited to insult, harass, or threaten other users or providers.",
      "In case of complaints, users may contact the company and provide the service provider’s ID.",
      "The company reserves the right to suspend or deny access at any time, without notice.",
      "Service providers must comply with applicable laws and regulations. The company disclaims liability for illegal practices.",
      "Users must respect the intellectual property rights of the app and service providers.",
      "The company may modify these terms without notice. Users should regularly review this section.",
      "Users are responsible for their own safety and privacy while using the app.",
      "Users must report any inappropriate or illegal content to the app administrators.",
      "The company does not guarantee the accuracy or completeness of information provided by service providers.",
      "Users must comply with the app’s terms and applicable local laws regarding road services.",
      "Misdemeanor of audio recording or photographing a person without their permission under Algerian Penal Code\n\nArticle 303 bis: (New)\nAnyone who deliberately violates the privacy of others using any technology is punished with imprisonment from six (6) months to three (3) years and a fine from 50,000 DZD to 300,000 DZD:\n1- By recording, capturing or transmitting private or secret conversations without the owner's consent.\n2- By recording, capturing or transmitting the image of a person in a private place without the owner's consent.\nAttempting to commit this offense is punishable with the same penalties as the completed crime.\nThe victim's pardon ends the criminal prosecution.\n\nArticle 303 bis 1: (New)\nThe same penalties shall apply to anyone who retains, distributes, allows access to, or uses by any means the recordings, images, or documents obtained through any of the acts referred to in Article 303 bis of the Penal Code."

    ]
